#: sdlc/processes/tracked-watch.bpmn:52
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Asked of the calling watch's `verdict`, not of the raw exit code. `no` is verdict == 'unknown': the job runs `exit 1` and no issue step runs, so the tracking issue is left untouched. `yes` is any other verdict, the guard on the label step and so on both issue paths."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/tracked-watch.bpmn:75
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Asked of the same `verdict`, once it is known. `no` is verdict == 'clean': the open tracking issue, if there is one, is closed. `yes` is a finding: the one open issue carrying the label is edited in place with the report as its body, or created if there is none. Neither branch fails the job."
msgstr ""

